WEBVTT

STYLE
::cue(c.color9CD5FF) { color: #9CD5FF; }
::cue(c.colora8c7fa) { color: #a8c7fa; }
::cue(c.credits) { color: #a8c7fa; font-size: 78%; }

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:07.000 line:5% align:center
<b><c.color9CD5FF>One Pace Premium</c></b>
Keep the project alive: <c.colora8c7fa>ko-fi.com/not6ip</c>

2
00:02:35.700 --> 00:02:37.340
Why did the video cut out?!

3
00:02:37.340 --> 00:02:39.020
Show us Marineford!

4
00:02:39.020 --> 00:02:40.540
Hurry and show it already!

5
00:02:40.540 --> 00:02:45.580
Something must have happened to their Visual Transponder Snails, there's nothing we can do!

6
00:02:45.580 --> 00:02:49.350
The Navy and Whitebeard made a deal? Can it be true?!

7
00:02:52.420 --> 00:02:53.750
Show us something!

8
00:02:54.100 --> 00:02:56.690
Did Whitebeard really sell out his companions?!

9
00:02:59.090 --> 00:03:01.060
What's going on in this war?!

10
00:03:02.830 --> 00:03:05.860
What will happen to the world?!

11
00:03:14.670 --> 00:03:18.330
What an annoying move by the Navy...

12
00:03:18.330 --> 00:03:20.680
I guess the show's over, huh?

13
00:03:20.680 --> 00:03:24.380
We sailed back here just so we could watch the war...

14
00:03:24.380 --> 00:03:26.160
now they're having trouble with the Visual Transponder Snails?

15
00:03:26.160 --> 00:03:28.190
There's no way that's the truth.

16
00:03:28.190 --> 00:03:29.720
Huh? It's not?

17
00:03:29.720 --> 00:03:34.690
You sure are an idiot. It's obvious that they're hiding something.

18
00:03:34.690 --> 00:03:37.970
Something they don't want pirates, or anyone else, to see...

19
00:03:47.640 --> 00:03:49.790
Captain Bonney...

20
00:03:49.790 --> 00:03:51.910
Shut up! Leave me alone!

21
00:03:51.910 --> 00:03:54.600
Whitebeard sold out his companions?

22
00:03:54.600 --> 00:04:00.050
Like hell. He's a legend because he never does anything like that.

23
00:04:00.190 --> 00:04:05.420
<b>Assault</b>

24
00:04:00.500 --> 00:04:01.880
Time to set sail, Bepo.

25
00:04:01.880 --> 00:04:03.520
Aye aye, Captain!

26
00:04:03.520 --> 00:04:05.420
Come with me, Jean Bart!

27
00:04:05.420 --> 00:04:08.760
That's right. It doesn't look like it'll be fixed anytime soon.

28
00:04:08.760 --> 00:04:12.560
Right now, there's no way to tell what's happening in Marineford.

29
00:04:16.740 --> 00:04:19.000
Meteor Volcano!

30
00:04:31.450 --> 00:04:33.820
We're not letting you escape!

31
00:04:33.820 --> 00:04:37.120
Melt the ice and take away their footing!

32
00:04:46.910 --> 00:04:49.010
T-The water...

33
00:04:49.540 --> 00:04:51.340
It's hot!

34
00:04:51.340 --> 00:04:53.570
The magma is making the water boil!

35
00:04:56.110 --> 00:04:57.680
Get out of the water, quickly!

36
00:04:58.980 --> 00:05:00.010
Hey, look!

37
00:05:11.310 --> 00:05:13.130
This way is blocked too!

38
00:05:17.700 --> 00:05:20.670
Is there nothing we can do against this wall?!

39
00:05:40.700 --> 00:05:42.320
Whitebeard...

40
00:05:45.620 --> 00:05:49.900
T-The Pops's attacks aren't working... That's no ordinary wall!

41
00:05:51.800 --> 00:05:54.400
Now, it's time to end this.

42
00:06:02.310 --> 00:06:05.130
The Moby Dick took a direct hit from the magma!

43
00:06:05.130 --> 00:06:06.850
Put out the fire!

44
00:06:06.850 --> 00:06:08.850
Hurry!

45
00:06:09.250 --> 00:06:11.020
You have to hold on!

46
00:06:13.750 --> 00:06:15.200
Don't let the ship sink!

47
00:06:15.200 --> 00:06:19.490
We're gonna travel the seas with our friends, and Ace, once more!

48
00:06:19.490 --> 00:06:23.260
Whitebeard. Your era is at an end!

49
00:06:39.510 --> 00:06:41.750
The Moby Dick...

50
00:06:42.230 --> 00:06:46.470
Damn it! Damn the Navy!

51
00:06:46.470 --> 00:06:49.250
That was our pride and joy!

52
00:06:50.590 --> 00:06:56.300
Damn! They destroyed our ship! The ship that's carried the Whitebeard Pirates for decades!

53
00:07:12.710 --> 00:07:15.330
Forgive me.

54
00:07:20.320 --> 00:07:23.660
We're losing our only way into the plaza!

55
00:07:25.060 --> 00:07:27.040
The plan is progressing smoothly.

56
00:07:27.040 --> 00:07:32.560
The execution of Portgas D. Ace... will proceed...

57
00:07:32.560 --> 00:07:35.100
immediately!

58
00:07:49.950 --> 00:07:51.750
We can't even see what's going on!

59
00:07:51.750 --> 00:07:54.050
There's no way we'll let them kill Ace!

60
00:07:54.050 --> 00:07:55.540
Yeah...

61
00:07:55.540 --> 00:07:57.440
There's still one way...

62
00:07:57.440 --> 00:07:59.160
One single path...

63
00:07:59.860 --> 00:08:02.200
The path that Oars made for us!

64
00:08:03.330 --> 00:08:07.430
If we go that way, we'll be killed. The Navy is sure to be waiting for us.

65
00:08:09.330 --> 00:08:11.680
This is no time to stand around and chat!

66
00:08:11.680 --> 00:08:15.100
Yeah... If we're gonna save Ace, that's the only way...

67
00:08:34.120 --> 00:08:37.100
Ace!

68
00:08:44.100 --> 00:08:45.500
Straw Hat...

69
00:08:45.500 --> 00:08:47.260
We'll go, too!

70
00:08:47.260 --> 00:08:51.440
Yeah!

71
00:08:58.200 --> 00:09:00.390
That route is far too obvious!

72
00:09:00.390 --> 00:09:04.200
It's not over yet! Hold them off as best as you can!

73
00:09:04.200 --> 00:09:05.020
Fire!

74
00:09:10.400 --> 00:09:14.960
There's no way the enemy would ignore the only opening!

75
00:09:14.960 --> 00:09:16.230
It's definitely a trap!

76
00:09:19.200 --> 00:09:20.240
Fire!

77
00:09:25.340 --> 00:09:27.020
Straw Hat-boy!

78
00:09:27.020 --> 00:09:27.950
Luffy-kun!

79
00:09:54.400 --> 00:09:58.410
Little Oars Jr.! He was still alive?!

80
00:09:59.140 --> 00:10:01.410
Ace... kun...

81
00:10:01.410 --> 00:10:03.820
Oars...

82
00:10:03.820 --> 00:10:08.560
I'm... gonna protect... Ace-kun...

83
00:10:08.560 --> 00:10:10.820
Oars!

84
00:10:14.190 --> 00:10:17.530
Captain Squard!

85
00:10:17.530 --> 00:10:20.110
You guys...

86
00:10:25.030 --> 00:10:26.970
Right!

87
00:10:29.740 --> 00:10:32.010
Are you alright, Luffy-kun?

88
00:10:32.010 --> 00:10:34.240
Really, how reckless can vyou get?

89
00:10:38.040 --> 00:10:39.680
Prepare to fire.

90
00:10:44.220 --> 00:10:46.000
Shoot!

91
00:10:48.830 --> 00:10:50.460
Oars!

92
00:10:51.800 --> 00:10:54.070
I've gotta do something...

93
00:10:54.070 --> 00:10:55.950
I've gotta hurry...

94
00:10:55.950 --> 00:10:59.370
They're gonna execute Ace!

95
00:10:59.370 --> 00:11:01.970
Yes, we must act quickly!

96
00:11:01.970 --> 00:11:03.940
Jinbe!

97
00:11:06.300 --> 00:11:08.560
I've got...

98
00:11:08.560 --> 00:11:10.980
a favor to ask!

99
00:11:10.980 --> 00:11:13.250
You sure are persistent...

100
00:11:13.250 --> 00:11:15.520
He's already half-dead! Finish him off!

101
00:11:15.750 --> 00:11:19.780
Oh, don't bother. I'll do it.

102
00:11:19.780 --> 00:11:21.230
Kizaru-san!

103
00:11:21.230 --> 00:11:26.230
We need to get the execution over with, and fast.

104
00:11:27.030 --> 00:11:33.770
At times like this, it's best to just pierce them right through the head...

105
00:11:33.770 --> 00:11:38.400
Ocean Current Shoulder Throw!

106
00:12:05.740 --> 00:12:07.590
Lu-

107
00:12:09.320 --> 00:12:10.890
Luffy!

108
00:12:18.520 --> 00:12:21.220
Oh, my. You finally made it here.

109
00:12:23.290 --> 00:12:27.880
Quite an entrance, son of Dragon.

110
00:12:29.330 --> 00:12:33.030
This youngster sure is scary...

111
00:12:39.370 --> 00:12:43.720
Ace's little brother just went straight over the wall!

112
00:12:43.720 --> 00:12:44.910
That kid...

113
00:12:50.150 --> 00:12:53.920
If nothing else, I praise your tenacity.

114
00:12:53.920 --> 00:12:58.820
But you're not ready for this stage yet.

115
00:12:58.820 --> 00:13:01.990
There's no way you can beat us, you know?

116
00:13:10.130 --> 00:13:12.640
Give Ace...

117
00:13:12.640 --> 00:13:17.480
back!

118
00:13:17.710 --> 00:13:22.010
He's just as reckless as his brother.

119
00:13:22.260 --> 00:13:24.650
Oars! Stay where you are.

120
00:13:24.650 --> 00:13:27.020
We'll need your strength.

121
00:13:27.020 --> 00:13:27.950
Pops...

122
00:13:28.180 --> 00:13:29.630
Jozu! Time for our trump card!

123
00:13:29.630 --> 00:13:30.390
Sure!

124
00:13:30.390 --> 00:13:32.590
All men, prepare yourselves!

125
00:13:32.590 --> 00:13:35.030
We're breaking into the plaza!

126
00:13:39.900 --> 00:13:42.000
Rubber-Rubber...

127
00:13:42.230 --> 00:13:45.690
Stamp Gatling!

128
00:14:22.810 --> 00:14:25.440
Gear Second!

129
00:14:28.280 --> 00:14:32.210
I don't have time to fight these guys!

130
00:14:32.620 --> 00:14:35.720
How cunning of him.

131
00:14:41.530 --> 00:14:44.360
Too slow.

132
00:14:56.710 --> 00:14:58.270
On my mark!

133
00:14:58.270 --> 00:14:59.670
Yes sir!

134
00:15:05.150 --> 00:15:06.310
Do it!

135
00:15:24.070 --> 00:15:28.880
Ace!!

136
00:15:45.780 --> 00:15:47.360
Who was that?!

137
00:15:52.960 --> 00:15:54.670
Bastard!

138
00:15:56.000 --> 00:16:02.610
Considering your old grudge against Whitebeard, I had thought we were lucky...

139
00:16:03.220 --> 00:16:05.810
Crocodile!

140
00:16:09.640 --> 00:16:10.580
Him!

141
00:16:12.860 --> 00:16:16.020
Huh... it wasn't my turn yet?

142
00:16:16.580 --> 00:16:23.190
You were hell-bent on killing the Pops.
 What's this sudden change of heart?

143
00:16:27.160 --> 00:16:30.070
That dying old man?

144
00:16:30.070 --> 00:16:32.600
I'll eliminate him later.

145
00:16:33.680 --> 00:16:35.640
But right now...

146
00:16:35.640 --> 00:16:40.110
I don't want to see you enjoying victory!

147
00:16:52.820 --> 00:16:55.620
Hey now, Crocodile-man!

148
00:16:55.620 --> 00:16:57.470
D-Doflamingo!

149
00:16:57.470 --> 00:17:01.170
So you're ditching me to team up with Whitebeard?

150
00:17:05.880 --> 00:17:09.870
It's enough to make a guy jealous, ya know...

151
00:17:13.000 --> 00:17:15.910
I don't team up with anybody.

152
00:17:16.440 --> 00:17:21.550
That's the same as brushing me off.

153
00:17:21.550 --> 00:17:23.490
More or less.

154
00:17:38.840 --> 00:17:42.470
I don't get what's going on... but we were saved.

155
00:17:42.820 --> 00:17:45.410
End of the line, Straw Hat!

156
00:17:46.040 --> 00:17:47.290
Die!

157
00:17:58.120 --> 00:17:59.990
Get out of...

158
00:18:00.820 --> 00:18:03.390
my way!

159
00:18:12.600 --> 00:18:14.420
Stop right there, Straw Hat!

160
00:18:14.880 --> 00:18:16.610
I will not let you go any further!

161
00:18:16.610 --> 00:18:18.110
Move it!

162
00:18:17.400 --> 00:18:17.900
Shave!

163
00:18:19.550 --> 00:18:20.340
Moon Walk!

164
00:18:22.380 --> 00:18:23.280
Iron Body...

165
00:18:23.780 --> 00:18:24.660
Smash!

166
00:18:31.540 --> 00:18:33.090
Rubber-Rubber...

167
00:18:33.090 --> 00:18:33.860
Iron Body!

168
00:18:34.580 --> 00:18:35.980
Bullet!

169
00:18:43.480 --> 00:18:45.670
Stop Straw Hat!

170
00:18:45.670 --> 00:18:47.540
Don't let him get any closer!

171
00:18:49.860 --> 00:18:51.180
Admiral Sakazuki!

172
00:19:04.640 --> 00:19:06.090
That hurts!

173
00:19:06.090 --> 00:19:07.850
Damn it!

174
00:19:07.850 --> 00:19:11.380
I'm indebted to your granddad, but...

175
00:19:11.380 --> 00:19:13.430
I have no choice!

176
00:19:13.430 --> 00:19:16.970
You have chosen your own death!

177
00:19:16.970 --> 00:19:20.140
You! Do not lay a hand on Luffy!

178
00:19:30.400 --> 00:19:31.470
Admiral!

179
00:19:32.260 --> 00:19:33.920
That's...

180
00:19:35.540 --> 00:19:38.660
The Commander of the First Division... Marco!

181
00:19:41.840 --> 00:19:43.660
Thanks for saving me.

182
00:19:44.540 --> 00:19:46.260
Don't mention it.

183
00:19:50.180 --> 00:19:53.010
Three people have penetrated the plaza!

184
00:19:53.010 --> 00:19:56.110
Devil Fruit users are passing over the walls!

185
00:20:00.820 --> 00:20:04.700
Cross the water and head for Oars!

186
00:20:05.320 --> 00:20:09.750
Whatever happens, get to the plaza!

187
00:20:10.460 --> 00:20:13.260
The pirates are getting desperate.

188
00:20:13.260 --> 00:20:15.180
Defend the gap in the walls!

189
00:20:15.180 --> 00:20:16.030
Yes sir!

190
00:20:20.100 --> 00:20:23.440
Even after losing their ships and their footing, they're still as frenzied as ever.

191
00:20:23.440 --> 00:20:25.580
Foolish pirates.

192
00:20:25.580 --> 00:20:28.070
They're sitting ducks! Fire!

193
00:21:24.200 --> 00:21:26.920
Everyone, get on board!

194
00:21:26.920 --> 00:21:28.930
Yeah!

195
00:21:29.600 --> 00:21:31.570
Hold on tight!

196
00:21:32.360 --> 00:21:34.140
No way! A ship...

197
00:21:34.960 --> 00:21:36.020
Big trouble!

198
00:21:36.020 --> 00:21:39.960
Another coated ship has emerged from the bay!

199
00:21:44.100 --> 00:21:45.140
Damn it!

200
00:21:45.140 --> 00:21:47.350
It was hiding underwater the whole time!

201
00:22:08.110 --> 00:22:12.380
I don't remember saying that we'd used all of our ships!

202
00:22:19.250 --> 00:22:21.320
It's a paddle ship!

203
00:22:21.320 --> 00:22:23.450
It's going to ram us!

204
00:22:24.200 --> 00:22:25.260
What?!

205
00:22:28.430 --> 00:22:32.160
Sink it! Just like the Moby Dick!

206
00:22:37.600 --> 00:22:39.940
No, not the ship!

207
00:22:39.940 --> 00:22:41.840
Shoot Oars!

208
00:22:41.840 --> 00:22:43.670
Huh? Oars?

209
00:22:44.460 --> 00:22:46.180
Too late!

210
00:22:46.180 --> 00:22:48.520
Here we go, everyone!

211
00:23:02.420 --> 00:23:05.640
H-He pulled the whole ship in!

212
00:23:05.640 --> 00:23:09.200
The intruders have breached the walls!

213
00:23:18.110 --> 00:23:20.970
We're in the plaza!

214
00:23:20.970 --> 00:23:24.680
Let's save Ace!

215
00:23:24.680 --> 00:23:27.750
Time to overthrow Navy HQ!

216
00:23:27.750 --> 00:23:31.220
Hang in there, Ace!

217
00:23:32.080 --> 00:23:33.740
They got us.

218
00:23:33.740 --> 00:23:39.230
There was one tiny mouse hole in the walls, and they swarmed right in.

219
00:23:40.020 --> 00:23:44.650
Those walls may wind up working against us.

220
00:23:44.650 --> 00:23:47.700
Pops!

221
00:23:47.700 --> 00:23:50.180
Whitebeard...

222
00:23:50.180 --> 00:23:54.880
Still got your head, Ace?

223
00:23:57.700 --> 00:24:00.380
We made it!

224
00:24:00.380 --> 00:24:05.640
Now Ace-kun can be resc-

225
00:24:09.230 --> 00:24:10.460
Oars!

226
00:24:16.620 --> 00:24:20.900
Save... Ace-kun...

227
00:24:34.040 --> 00:24:36.250
Oars...

228
00:25:23.400 --> 00:25:27.060
Whitebeard has entered the plaza!

229
00:25:33.080 --> 00:25:37.080
Stand back, my sons.

230
00:26:09.860 --> 00:26:11.870
Men!

231
00:26:11.870 --> 00:26:18.360
Rescue Ace, and destroy the Navy!

232
00:26:24.960 --> 00:26:26.960
Garp...

233
00:26:26.960 --> 00:26:28.500
Yeah.

234
00:26:32.360 --> 00:26:38.040
It looks like even we have to take a hand in this!

235
